   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Three genders",
     "texto": [
      "German has three genders: masculine (**der**), feminine (**die**) and neuter (**das**). They don't match English, nor do they follow a clear logic: «the key» is **der Schlüssel** and «the book» is **das Buch**.",
      "That's why you learn every noun **with its article**. In this course's cards, you'll see it in parentheses.",
      "The indefinite article: **ein** for masculine and neuter, **eine** for feminine."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "The articles",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Masculine",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Feminine",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Neuter",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Plural",
       "lengua": "estudio"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
