    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The plural and «What is this?»",
     "texto": [
      "In the nominative and accusative, the plural article is **die**, whatever the singular gender: **die Bücher**, **die Taschen**. In the plural dative it changes to **den**, and the noun usually adds **-n**: **mit den Büchern**; if it already ends in -n or -s, another one isn't added. You have to learn each noun's plural: Buch → **Bücher**, Tasche → **Taschen**, Schlüssel → **Schlüssel** (doesn't change).",
      "**Was ist das?** = What is this? You reply with **Das ist ein Buch** or, in the plural, **Das sind Bücher**.",
      "To replace a thing, use the pronoun for its gender: **er** (der), **sie** (die), **es** (das): **Das Handy ist neu. Es ist klein.**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Colors",
     "texto": [
      "After «sein», colors don't change: **Die Tasche ist schwarz**, **Das Buch ist rot**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
